# Fleet SSH access registry: the reviewed public keys that may be granted
# inbound SSH access to a machine running `atyrode tunnel`. Public material
# only; private keys live in the Bitwarden vault (see docs/git-keys.md).
#
# A key becomes grantable only through a reviewed commit here, exactly as a
# signing key becomes trusted only through a reviewed commit in
# modules/home/git/allowed-signers. Registration is not access: it authorizes nothing
# by itself. `atyrode tunnel grant NAME` records a local, usually expiring
# grant on one machine, and `atyrode tunnel` renders that machine's
# ~/.ssh/authorized_keys from this registry and its grant state. See
# docs/atyrode.md ("Fleet SSH access").
#
# One line per key, whitespace-separated:
#
#   NAME  ROLE  KEYTYPE  BASE64-KEY
#
# NAME   stable identifier `atyrode tunnel grant|revoke` accepts, and the
#        comment written into the rendered authorized_keys line.
# ROLE   `primary` or `revocable`. Exactly one line is `primary`: it is
#        rendered on every machine with no expiry and `tunnel revoke` refuses
#        it, so a mistaken revocation can never lock the operator out of a
#        machine reachable only over SSH. Everything else is `revocable`.
# KEYTYPE/BASE64-KEY  the first two fields of the key's authorized_keys line.
#
# The rendered file is generated from this registry alone, which is what stops
# a duplicated key, or one split across two lines that sshd silently discards
# as malformed, from reaching an authorized_keys file.

